  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So my idea goes like this: when people touch their finger to the trackpad and don't move it, that won't change their gesture, and when they move their finger like a certain small amount then it will change their gesture (and act like normal with the position of your thumb on the circle deciding what gesture is shown), if they press the trackpad down at any time, the movement system works like normal but doesn't change their hand gesture, and if they stop pressing down on the trackpad but keep their finger touching it, it will actually keep/\"lock\" their hand gesture until they remove their finger from the trackpad and touch and move on it again, but they can still move and turn like normal (for instance they need to adjust their position a little more, so it locks their gesture until they stop touching the trackpad).\nAlso of note: At any time, if they press the trigger or grip/squeeze buttons, it will act like normal and open/make-a-fist-with their hand until they let go of said buttons and their hand will return to a normal idle gesture, and go into the state where they have to take their finger off and touch the trackpad again to set their hand gesture again.",
